# The qualified and unqualified senses of "knowing" are already split into separate claims (knowing_known vs knowing). The move between them is stated openly as premise R1 (S5), so no single claim shifts sense.
# S9's "you said just now that you were knowing" recalls Socrates' qualified admission in S4. Even so, the argument uses it in the unqualified sense throughout, so I have treated "knowing" as one sense.
